Rank":60,"winningTimeRank":44,"winningTimeRankDir":19,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1948,"mensWinner":"Bill Savage","mensTime":"07:13:52"}},"narrative":"The 1990 Comrades Marathon was the 65th running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 87.400 km. The race was held on Thursday, 31 May. Conditions: Cloudless and very hot. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nBruce FORDYCE claimed the men's title in 05:40:25, ahead of Hoseah TJALE (05:45:19) and Meshack RADEBE (05:45:40). Naidene STEWART won the women's race in 07:02:00, followed by Annette SCHOEMAN (07:07:35).\n\nNaidene STEWART's 07:02:00 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1948 (Bill Savage, 07:13:52).\n\nFrom a field of 11,616 entries, 10,264 runners crossed the finish line (88.4% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 9,615 men and 649 women (6.3% female). The average finish time was 09:29:42.\n\nMedals awarded: 13 Gold, 847 Silver, 9,404 Bronze. 3,153 runners (30.7%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Sampie SAMSODIEN in 10:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 1988, the field was 5.5% smaller.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 26% of the finishers, with 7,612 seniors (avg 09:25:54) and 2,652 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}